Excuse me.

256
00:20:51,089 --> 00:20:52,548
Dr. Gordon.

257
00:20:53,299 --> 00:20:54,842
I'm Detective Tapp.

258
00:20:54,926 --> 00:20:56,594
This is Detective Sing. City homicide.

259
00:20:56,928 --> 00:20:58,346
Very impressive.

260
00:20:58,930 --> 00:21:00,348
Oh, thank you.

261
00:21:01,432 --> 00:21:02,976
I do my best.

262
00:21:05,395 --> 00:21:08,147
Sorry to interrupt
you while you're working.

263
00:21:08,856 --> 00:21:10,441
It's fine. Now,
how can I help you gentlemen?

264
00:21:11,359 --> 00:21:13,820
Are you able to tell us
where you were between the hours

265
00:21:13,903 --> 00:21:16,280
of 11 p.m. And 1 a.m. Last night, Doctor?

266
00:21:17,532 --> 00:21:19,325
Why is it that you're interested?

267
00:21:19,659 --> 00:21:21,953
We'd like to ask
you a few questions about it.

268
00:21:23,037 --> 00:21:26,582
For your sake, I think it's best
if we do it down at the station.

269
00:21:26,874 --> 00:21:28,334
Would you like to follow us there?

270
00:21:28,751 --> 00:21:31,337
I'm afraid that's
quite out of the question.

271
00:21:31,754 --> 00:21:34,048
I can't just leave. I have work to do.

272
00:21:34,132 --> 00:21:35,800
Plus my wife has the car today.

273
00:21:35,883 --> 00:21:37,510
That's ok. You can ride with us...

274
00:21:38,761 --> 00:21:39,637
Doc.

275
00:21:43,933 --> 00:21:48,146
Ha ha. I'm sorry.
You'll have to tell me again.

276
00:21:48,229 --> 00:21:50,023
What is this all about?

277
00:21:51,315 --> 00:21:53,026
Is this yours, Doctor?

278
00:22:05,955 --> 00:22:07,248
<i> So, you have no idea</i>

279
00:22:07,331 --> 00:22:09,625
how your penlight
showed up at the murder scene?

280
00:22:09,709 --> 00:22:11,502
Of course not, Brett.

281
00:22:14,964 --> 00:22:16,007
Well, I have to ask...

282
00:22:16,799 --> 00:22:18,009
what were you doing last night?

283
00:22:21,137 --> 00:22:22,847
I was seeing someone.

284
00:22:23,806 --> 00:22:25,558
Who?

285
00:22:29,812 --> 00:22:32,065
Look, if you can't be honest with me--

286
00:22:32,148 --> 00:22:34,233
I was visiting
someone. It wasn't a patient.

287
00:22:34,567 --> 00:22:35,735
<i>All right?</i>

288
00:22:39,447 --> 00:22:40,531
What am I gonna do?

289
00:22:40,615 --> 00:22:42,825
Well, as your lawyer and your friend,

290
00:22:42,909 --> 00:22:47,330
my advice to you is to bite the bullet
and give them your alibi now,

291
00:22:48,956 --> 00:22:50,583
<i>because no one's gonna believe you later.</i>

292
00:22:56,255 --> 00:22:57,965
That was 5 months ago.

293
00:23:01,969 --> 00:23:04,013
He tried to set me up for murder.

294
00:23:08,184 --> 00:23:09,102
Ok.

295
00:23:10,353 --> 00:23:12,855
We checked your alibi. It holds up.

296
00:23:12,939 --> 00:23:15,525
Good. Can I go home now?

297
00:23:16,442 --> 00:23:19,153
<i>We have one of</i>
<i>the victims who managed to escape.</i>

298
00:23:19,904 --> 00:23:22,323
<i>We want to know if</i>
<i>you wouldn't mind sticking around</i>

299
00:23:22,406 --> 00:23:24,242
<i>and listening to her testimony.</i>

300
00:23:24,325 --> 00:23:27,954
-<i>Maybe it'll trigger something.</i>
-I'd like to help, really, but--

301
00:23:28,037 --> 00:23:29,539
Well, we'd really appreciate it.

302
00:23:30,498 --> 00:23:31,791
<i>She's the only one who made it.</i>

303
00:23:31,874 --> 00:23:33,084
Ok.

304
00:23:39,215 --> 00:23:40,174
Amanda...

305
00:23:41,759 --> 00:23:46,556
in your own time...
tell me the first thing you remember.

306
00:24:01,279 --> 00:24:06,033
<i>I woke up.</i>
<i>All I could taste was blood...</i>

307
00:24:07,869 --> 00:24:08,911
<i>And metal.</i>

308
00:24:38,065 --> 00:24:40,067
Hello, Amanda.

309
00:24:40,151 --> 00:24:41,861
You don't know me,

310
00:24:42,653 --> 00:24:44,155
<i>but I know you.</i>

311
00:24:44,363 --> 00:24:46,407
I want to play a game.

312
00:24:46,490 --> 00:24:48,534
<i>Here's what happens if you lose.</i>

313
00:24:49,744 --> 00:24:53,789
<i>The device you're wearing is hooked into</i>
<i>your upper and lower jaws.</i>

314
00:24:54,540 --> 00:24:56,626
When the timer on the back goes off,

315
00:24:56,709 --> 00:25:00,046
<i>your mouth will be</i>
<i>permanently ripped open.</i>

316
00:25:00,129 --> 00:25:03,174
<i>Think of it like a reverse bear trap.</i>

317
00:25:04,258 --> 00:25:06,677
Here, I'll show you.

318
00:25:18,940 --> 00:25:22,109
There's only one key to open the device.

319
00:25:22,568 --> 00:25:25,279
It's in the stomach of your dead cellmate.

320
00:25:27,365 --> 00:25:28,991
Look around, Amanda.

321
00:25:29,075 --> 00:25:30,368
<i>Know that I'm not lying.</i>

322
00:25:31,160 --> 00:25:32,495
You better hurry up.

323
00:25:33,454 --> 00:25:36,916
Live or die. Make your choice.

324
00:25:56,310 --> 00:25:59,063
Aah! No! Aah!

325
00:26:15,121 --> 00:26:16,914
And then I saw the body.

326
00:26:41,147 --> 00:26:43,316
There was a knife.

327
00:27:14,221 --> 00:27:16,932
<i>He'd been injected</i>
<i>with an opiate overdose.</i>

328
00:27:18,309 --> 00:27:20,603
Couldn't move or feel much of anything.

329
00:27:23,105 --> 00:27:25,316
You mean... he was alive?

330
00:27:25,733 --> 00:27:26,901
Was.

331
00:27:28,611 --> 00:27:30,654
What happened after you took it off?

332
00:28:28,546 --> 00:28:29,797
Congratulations.

333
00:28:30,214 --> 00:28:31,757
<i>You are still alive.</i>

334
00:28:32,842 --> 00:28:36,804
Most people are so ungrateful to be alive,

335
00:28:36,887 --> 00:28:38,222
<i>but not you.</i>

336
00:28:38,556 --> 00:28:40,141
Not anymore.

337
00:28:46,313 --> 00:28:48,607
You are, in fact, a drug addict.

338
00:28:49,483 --> 00:28:50,818
Isn't that right, Mandy?

339
00:28:53,154 --> 00:28:55,406
Do you think that is why he picked you?

340
00:29:02,496 --> 00:29:04,415
Are you grateful, Mandy?

341
00:29:09,462 --> 00:29:10,754
He...

342
00:29:11,547 --> 00:29:13,090
helped me.

343
00:29:51,337 --> 00:29:52,796
Are you sure it's him?

344
00:29:54,423 --> 00:29:58,052
-Yeah, I'm sure.
-How do I know you're telling the truth?

345
00:29:59,053 --> 00:30:01,305
You could be the one
who put me in this room.

346
00:30:01,388 --> 00:30:05,559
I'm in exactly
the same situation that you're in.

347
00:30:05,643 --> 00:30:07,353
Wrong. Wrong!

348
00:30:07,436 --> 00:30:10,272
You've got one thing I don't--information!

349
00:30:10,356 --> 00:30:11,607
You know who did this.

350
00:30:11,690 --> 00:30:15,528
Now, you either tell
me what is really going on,

351
00:30:15,611 --> 00:30:17,947
or I'll cut you with this! You hear me?
I'll cu--

352
00:30:25,287 --> 00:30:25,996
What?

353
00:30:26,330 --> 00:30:27,331
It's a 2-way mirror.

354
00:30:57,361 --> 00:30:59,655
<i>I can see you.</i>

355
00:31:00,239 --> 00:31:01,657
So, that's what this is--

356
00:31:02,324 --> 00:31:03,409
reality TV.

357
00:31:04,118 --> 00:31:06,537
<i>Don't look at me. I can't help you.</i>

358
00:31:06,620 --> 00:31:08,622
Can you hear me in there, huh?

359
00:31:08,706 --> 00:31:10,374
<i>I'm having a blast.</i>

360
00:31:10,457 --> 00:31:12,710
This is the most fun
I've had without lubricant.

361
00:31:13,794 --> 00:31:15,963
Make sure you're getting everything.

362
00:31:18,757 --> 00:31:21,135
That's not gonna do anything.

363
00:31:22,886 --> 00:31:25,931
-You just want to leave it running on us?
-Well, you won't stop it.

364
00:31:26,640 --> 00:31:28,267
That's why we can't
cut through these chains.

365
00:31:28,392 --> 00:31:30,227
It's why you won't break that glass.

366
00:31:30,519 --> 00:31:33,439
Every possible angle
has been pre-thought out by him.

367
00:31:33,522 --> 00:31:35,065
You make it sound
like you admire this prick.

368
00:31:36,609 --> 00:31:37,901
To overcome something,

369
00:31:37,985 --> 00:31:40,487
you have to understand
what a perfect engine it is.

370
00:31:40,571 --> 00:31:43,073
That's how you fight disease.

371
00:31:43,157 --> 00:31:46,577
<i>The tape told us to find an "x."</i>

372
00:31:46,660 --> 00:31:48,662
That "x" has to be somewhere in this room.

373
00:31:48,746 --> 00:31:50,456
<i>Help me find it.</i>

374
00:31:50,539 --> 00:31:52,416
How can you be the calm Doctor guy

375
00:31:52,499 --> 00:31:55,127
<i>when your wife and kid are out there?</i>
<i>He's got them, too.</i>

376
00:31:55,210 --> 00:31:56,545
<i>He could be doing</i>
<i>anything to them right now.</i>

377
00:31:56,629 --> 00:31:58,339
<i>You thinking about that?</i>

378
00:31:58,422 --> 00:32:00,924
I am thinking about that.

379
00:32:06,639 --> 00:32:09,725
I've been thinking about
the last thing I said to my daughter.

380
00:33:54,079 --> 00:33:57,374
Diana, honey, are you ok?

381
00:33:58,250 --> 00:34:00,586
Diana, honey, can you hear me?

382
00:34:00,669 --> 00:34:01,837
Mommy.

383
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:03,797
What is it, sweetpea?

384
00:34:03,881 --> 00:34:06,258
There's a man in my room.

385
00:34:06,717 --> 00:34:10,637
Oh, honey, are you sure
he's not just hiding in your imagination?

386
00:34:10,721 --> 00:34:11,889
He talked to me.

387
00:34:13,682 --> 00:34:16,560
Ok. I'll come and check your room.

388
00:34:17,144 --> 00:34:20,355
I want daddy. He'll get the scary man.

389
00:34:21,982 --> 00:34:23,567
All right, if you want.

390
00:34:24,067 --> 00:34:25,486
Come on.

391
00:34:27,780 --> 00:34:32,075
Larry, sorry to bother you,
but your daughter had a bad dream again.

392
00:34:32,159 --> 00:34:33,827
Just a minute.

393
00:34:34,661 --> 00:34:36,121
She wants you to check her room.

394
00:34:36,205 --> 00:34:40,667
Hmm? Mm-hmm.
Just got to finish this paragraph.

395
00:34:43,670 --> 00:34:46,882
Come on, sweetie. I'll check with you.

396
00:34:48,759 --> 00:34:50,385
Nope. I'm done.

397
00:34:52,721 --> 00:34:55,724
See? There's no one in your room.

398
00:34:56,725 --> 00:34:59,770
There's no such thing as the bad man.

399
00:34:59,853 --> 00:35:01,563
Now can you go to sleep?

400
00:35:01,647 --> 00:35:03,649
-<i>I'm still scared.</i>
-You are?

401
00:35:03,982 --> 00:35:06,527
Give me your tootsie.

402
00:35:06,944 --> 00:35:07,945
Uh!

403
00:35:08,403 --> 00:35:09,905
Oh, what a big tootsie.

404
00:35:10,781 --> 00:35:12,074
Remember this one?

405
00:35:13,575 --> 00:35:14,952
This little piggy went to Market.

406
00:35:15,035 --> 00:35:16,954
This little piggy stayed home.

407
00:35:17,579 --> 00:35:19,414
This little piggy had roast beef.

408
00:35:19,790 --> 00:35:21,917
This little piggy had none.

409
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,086
This little piggy ran...

410
00:35:24,169 --> 00:35:27,130
whee... all the way home!

411
00:35:30,592 --> 00:35:31,969
I hate that thing.

412
00:35:32,052 --> 00:35:34,805
Well, I have to go to work, sweetheart.

413
00:35:34,888 --> 00:35:36,890
You know what daddy's job is like.

414
00:35:36,974 --> 00:35:38,308
Now, come on.

415
00:35:39,059 --> 00:35:40,519
Let's see.

416
00:35:42,062 --> 00:35:43,814
Try and get some sleep now, ok?

417
00:35:44,648 --> 00:35:45,649
Ok.

418
00:35:51,029 --> 00:35:53,824
You're not gonna leave us,
are you, daddy?

419
00:35:55,784 --> 00:35:56,910
What?

420
00:35:59,037 --> 00:36:00,247
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

421
00:36:01,707 --> 00:36:03,876
You mean leave you and mommy?

422
00:36:05,794 --> 00:36:08,046
No. No, sweetheart. I...

423
00:36:08,130 --> 00:36:10,382
I would never do that.

424
00:36:10,757 --> 00:36:12,718
Who gave you that idea?

425
00:36:13,760 --> 00:36:14,678
No one.

426
00:36:16,054 --> 00:36:18,599
Well, it's not true, ok?

427
00:36:19,808 --> 00:36:20,726
<i>Ok.</i>

428
00:36:20,809 --> 00:36:21,935
How much do I love you?

429
00:36:22,895 --> 00:36:24,146
Love you very much.

430
00:36:24,229 --> 00:36:26,064
That's right. That's right.

431
00:36:26,732 --> 00:36:29,276
-Good night, sweetie.
-Good night, daddy.

432
00:36:34,197 --> 00:36:35,365
Tomorrow...

433
00:36:36,325 --> 00:36:38,076
I'll read you your favorite story.

434
00:36:38,160 --> 00:36:39,369
Ok.

435
00:36:39,453 --> 00:36:40,412
Ok.

436
00:36:40,495 --> 00:36:42,039
<i>I don't know how much</i>
<i>longer I can do this, Larry.</i>

437
00:36:42,122 --> 00:36:43,332
Do what? What are you talking about?

438
00:36:43,415 --> 00:36:45,751
How can you walk through life
pretending that you're happy?

439
00:36:45,834 --> 00:36:48,545
-I am happy.
-That is complete bullshit.

440
00:36:49,046 --> 00:36:52,090
<i>I would rather you just break down</i>
<i>and tell me that you hate me.</i>

441
00:36:52,174 --> 00:36:54,760
<i>At least there would</i>
<i>be some passion in it.</i>

442
00:36:57,930 --> 00:37:00,057
Would you like to see her?

443
00:37:17,157 --> 00:37:18,617
<i>She's beautiful.</i>

444
00:37:18,700 --> 00:37:19,993
<i>Thank you.</i>

445
00:37:21,620 --> 00:37:23,372
You gonna have any more kids?

446
00:37:23,455 --> 00:37:25,916
Ah, we've... talked about it,

447
00:37:25,999 --> 00:37:29,795
but with our schedules, it's...

448
00:37:30,796 --> 00:37:32,839
it's difficult enough
to concentrate on one.

449
00:37:34,591 --> 00:37:37,052
So, where's the lucky wife?

450
00:37:38,303 --> 00:37:40,514
There's another picture
behind the one you're looking at.

451
00:37:40,764 --> 00:37:42,391
<i>It's my favorite one because...</i>

452
00:37:43,642 --> 00:37:44,977
<i>we're all in it together.</i>

453
00:37:45,060 --> 00:37:48,480
Someone, usually
me, has to hold the camera,

454
00:37:48,563 --> 00:37:50,565
which means I'm
always missing from the photos.

455
00:38:00,158 --> 00:38:01,743
<i>"X" Marks the spot.</i>

456
00:38:01,827 --> 00:38:06,873
<i>Sometimes you see</i>
<i>more with your eyes shut.</i>

457
00:38:08,125 --> 00:38:09,710
It's, uh...

458
00:38:09,793 --> 00:38:10,794
it's not here.

459
00:38:11,753 --> 00:38:12,838
What?

460
00:38:13,046 --> 00:38:14,881
This photo you're talking about

461
00:38:14,965 --> 00:38:16,049
is not here.

462
00:38:16,341 --> 00:38:18,468
Really? Are you sure?

463
00:38:18,552 --> 00:38:21,888
Yeah. Just... Oh!

464
00:38:35,152 --> 00:38:36,570
Why, he...he must have taken it. I...

465
00:38:37,070 --> 00:38:39,656
How can you walk through life
pretending that you're happy?

466
00:38:39,740 --> 00:38:40,907
I am happy.

467
00:38:40,991 --> 00:38:42,617
That is complete bullshit.

468
00:38:42,701 --> 00:38:45,203
I'd rather you break down
and tell me that you hated me.

469
00:38:45,287 --> 00:38:46,663
At least there would
be some passion in it.

470
00:38:50,542 --> 00:38:52,586
We'll talk about this later, ok?

471
00:38:56,339 --> 00:38:57,591
Just leave.

472
00:39:31,917 --> 00:39:34,503
<i>Good night, little girl.</i>

473
00:39:39,341 --> 00:39:41,301
-Aah!
-Diana?

474
00:39:42,761 --> 00:39:43,678
<i>Diana?</i>

475
00:39:47,849 --> 00:39:50,602
-Aah!
-Diana!

476
00:40:26,680 --> 00:40:28,223
Don't you hurt her!

477
00:40:28,306 --> 00:40:32,269
Get it away from
her! Get it away from her!

478
00:40:35,939 --> 00:40:38,316
Mommy!

479
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:40,861
Mommy!

480
00:40:40,944 --> 00:40:42,195
Mommy!

481
00:40:42,279 --> 00:40:44,990
Mommy!

482
00:40:56,376 --> 00:41:02,674
Let go of my daughter! Let go of her!

483
00:41:27,365 --> 00:41:32,162
<i> Oh, you little man, I see you.</i>

484
00:41:35,498 --> 00:41:41,129
<i>Does Dr. Gordon know</i>
<i>you're at home with his wife?</i>

485
00:41:41,213 --> 00:41:44,674
<i>I know you know something.</i>

486
00:41:49,429 --> 00:41:51,431
What are you doing in there?

487
00:41:52,307 --> 00:41:54,059
<i>Waiting for the Doctor?</i>

488
00:41:54,309 --> 00:41:57,479
I'm waiting for the Doctor, too.

489
00:42:08,490 --> 00:42:11,243
I never should have let you go.

490
00:42:20,502 --> 00:42:23,171
<i> There was someone</i>
<i>standing outside here watching.</i>

491
00:42:23,255 --> 00:42:25,090
<i>I want to play a game.</i>

492
00:42:26,633 --> 00:42:31,012
<i>I think we're</i>
<i>gonna be here for a while, Sing.</i>

493
00:42:36,434 --> 00:42:37,811
<i>Dr. Gordon, are you able to tell us</i>

494
00:42:37,894 --> 00:42:38,937
<i>where you were last night?</i>

495
00:42:39,020 --> 00:42:43,400
<i>You have no idea how your penlight</i>
<i>showed up at the murder scene?</i>

496
00:42:43,483 --> 00:42:44,484
We checked your alibi. It holds up.

497
00:42:44,567 --> 00:42:46,152
Isn't that right, Doctor?

498
00:42:46,236 --> 00:42:48,571
<i>I never should have let you go.</i>

499
00:42:53,243 --> 00:42:54,786
Here we are.

500
00:42:55,996 --> 00:42:57,539
That was...

501
00:42:58,456 --> 00:43:00,917
quite an amazing story
that poor woman told.

502
00:43:16,516 --> 00:43:17,517
Look, I'm...

503
00:43:18,977 --> 00:43:21,938
I'm sorry I can't be of
more help to your investigation.

504
00:43:23,732 --> 00:43:26,651
You know, we arrested a Dentist last week.

505
00:43:26,735 --> 00:43:29,279
He liked to play with kids a bit too much.

506
00:43:30,322 --> 00:43:32,032
He lived 2 blocks from here.

507
00:43:33,366 --> 00:43:37,996
The sewer lines run
under this neighborhood, too...Doctor.

508
00:44:02,437 --> 00:44:06,232
<i>Hello, Amanda. You don't know me,</i>

509
00:44:06,316 --> 00:44:08,318
<i>but I know you.</i>

510
00:44:08,401 --> 00:44:10,487
<i>I want to play a game.</i>

511
00:44:10,570 --> 00:44:12,947
<i>Here's what happens if you lose.</i>

512
00:44:15,825 --> 00:44:19,788
